{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794739048,"nonce":"svAKeRHiyTPQz0GsmUog2hPS3eo=","message":"The benchmark.\n\nCargo.toml:\n\n```toml\n[package]\nname = \"crossing\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]\nhxn = { git = \"https://github.com/hx-n/hxn.git\", tag = \"v0.3.2\" }\nobjc2 = \"0.6\"\nobjc2-foundation = { version = \"0.3\", default-features = false, features = [\"std\", \"NSString\", \"NSError\"] }\nobjc2-metal = { version = \"0.3\", default-features = false, features = [\n    \"std\", \"MTLDevice\", \"MTLBuffer\", \"MTLResource\", \"MTLAllocation\", \"MTLTexture\", \"MTLTypes\", \"MTLPixelFormat\",\n    \"MTLLibrary\", \"MTLCommandQueue\", \"MTLCommandBuffer\", \"MTLCommandEncoder\", \"MTLRenderCommandEncoder\",\n    \"MTLRenderPipeline\", \"MTLRenderPass\", \"MTLPipeline\",\n] }\n```\n\nsrc/lib.rs:\n\n```rust\n//! Times the cost of a call from Haxe into Rust, and of encoding Metal draws from Haxe.\n\nuse std::ffi::c_void;\nuse std::ptr::NonNull;\n\nuse objc2::rc::Retained;\nuse objc2::runtime::ProtocolObject;\nuse objc2_foundation::NSString;\nuse objc2_metal::*;\n\n/// Calls that do next to nothing, so a loop of them times the crossing itself.\npub struct Probe {\n    count: i32,\n}\n\nimpl Probe {\n    pub fn new() -\u003e Self {\n        Self { count: 0 }\n    }\n\n    /// A static function with no arguments.\n    pub fn nothing() {}\n\n    /// A method: the handle is looked up and borrowed.\n    pub fn touch(\u0026self) {}\n\n    /// An int in and out, through an exclusive borrow.\n    pub fn add(\u0026mut self, value: i32) -\u003e i32 {\n        self.count = self.count.wrapping_add(value);\n        self.count\n    }\n\n    /// A byte slice in.\n    pub fn bytes(\u0026self, bytes: \u0026[u8]) -\u003e i32 {\n        bytes.len() as i32\n    }\n}\n\nstruct Owned\u003cT: ?Sized\u003e(Retained\u003cT\u003e);\nunsafe impl\u003cT: ?Sized\u003e Send for Owned\u003cT\u003e {}\nunsafe impl\u003cT: ?Sized\u003e Sync for Owned\u003cT\u003e {}\n\n/// A render pass into an offscreen texture, whose draws are encoded in the ways being compared.\npub struct Pass {\n    queue: Owned\u003cProtocolObject\u003cdyn MTLCommandQueue\u003e\u003e,\n    target: Owned\u003cProtocolObject\u003cdyn MTLTexture\u003e\u003e,\n    pipeline: Owned\u003cProtocolObject\u003cdyn MTLRenderPipelineState\u003e\u003e,\n    commands: Option\u003cOwned\u003cProtocolObject\u003cdyn MTLCommandBuffer\u003e\u003e\u003e,\n    encoder: Option\u003cOwned\u003cProtocolObject\u003cdyn MTLRenderCommandEncoder\u003e\u003e\u003e,\n}\n\nconst SHADER: \u0026str = \"\nusing namespace metal;\nstruct Out { float4 position [[position]]; float size [[point_size]]; };\nvertex Out point_vertex(uint id [[vertex_id]], constant float4\u0026 offset [[buffer(0)]]) {\n    Out out; out.position = float4(0, 0, 0, 1) + offset; out.size = 1; return out;\n}\nfragment float4 point_fragment() { return float4(1); }\n\";\n\nimpl Pass {\n    pub fn new() -\u003e Result\u003cPass, String\u003e {\n        let device = MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice().ok_or(\"no Metal device\")?;\n        let queue = device.newCommandQueue().ok_or(\"no queue\")?;\n        let library = device\n            .newLibraryWithSource_options_error(\u0026NSString::from_str(SHADER), None)\n            .map_err(|e| e.localizedDescription().to_string())?;\n        let function = |name: \u0026str| library.newFunctionWithName(\u0026NSString::from_str(name)).ok_or(\"no function\");\n        let descriptor = MTLRenderPipelineDescriptor::new();\n        let (vertex, fragment) = (function(\"point_vertex\")?, function(\"point_fragment\")?);\n        descriptor.setVertexFunction(Some(\u0026vertex));\n        descriptor.setFragmentFunction(Some(\u0026fragment));\n        unsafe { descriptor.colorAttachments().objectAtIndexedSubscript(0) }.setPixelFormat(MTLPixelFormat::RGBA8Unorm);\n        let pipeline = device\n            .newRenderPipelineStateWithDescriptor_error(\u0026descriptor)\n            .map_err(|e| e.localizedDescription().to_string())?;\n        let texture = unsafe {\n            MTLTextureDescriptor::texture2DDescriptorWithPixelFormat_width_height_mipmapped(MTLPixelFormat::RGBA8Unorm, 64, 64, false)\n        };\n        texture.setUsage(MTLTextureUsage::RenderTarget);\n        texture.setStorageMode(MTLStorageMode::Private);\n        let target = device.newTextureWithDescriptor(\u0026texture).ok_or(\"no texture\")?;\n        Ok(Pass { queue: Owned(queue), target: Owned(target), pipeline: Owned(pipeline), commands: None, encoder: None })\n    }\n\n    /// Starts a command buffer and a render pass with the pipeline set.\n    pub fn begin(\u0026mut self) -\u003e Result\u003c(), String\u003e {\n        let commands = self.queue.0.commandBuffer().ok_or(\"no command buffer\")?;\n        let pass = MTLRenderPassDescriptor::new();\n        let color = unsafe { pass.colorAttachments().objectAtIndexedSubscript(0) };\n        color.setTexture(Some(\u0026self.target.0));\n        color.setLoadAction(MTLLoadAction::Clear);\n        color.setStoreAction(MTLStoreAction::Store);\n        let encoder = commands.renderCommandEncoderWithDescriptor(\u0026pass).ok_or(\"no encoder\")?;\n        encoder.setRenderPipelineState(\u0026self.pipeline.0);\n        self.commands = Some(Owned(commands));\n        self.encoder = Some(Owned(encoder));\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    /// Sets the vertex offset: one command, as a driver's `setVertexBytes` is.\n    pub fn set_offset(\u0026mut self, x: f64) {\n        self.offset(x as f32);\n    }\n\n    /// Draws one point: one command, as a driver's `draw` is.\n    pub fn draw(\u0026mut self) {\n        self.point();\n    }\n\n    /// Both commands in one call.\n    pub fn set_and_draw(\u0026mut self, x: f64) {\n        self.offset(x as f32);\n        self.point();\n    }\n\n    /// Draws `count` points encoded in Rust alone: what Metal itself costs.\n    pub fn draws_in_rust(\u0026mut self, count: i32) {\n        for i in 0..count {\n            self.offset((i % 64) as f32 / 64.0);\n            self.point();\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Replays a stream of draws Haxe wrote: one little-endian f32 offset per draw.\n    pub fn replay(\u0026mut self, stream: \u0026[u8]) {\n        for chunk in stream.chunks_exact(4) {\n            self.offset(f32::from_le_bytes([chunk[0], chunk[1], chunk[2], chunk[3]]));\n            self.point();\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Ends the pass, commits it, and waits for the GPU.\n    #[hxn(blocking)]\n    pub fn finish(\u0026mut self) {\n        if let Some(encoder) = self.encoder.take() {\n            encoder.0.endEncoding();\n        }\n        if let Some(commands) = self.commands.take() {\n            commands.0.commit();\n            commands.0.waitUntilCompleted();\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Pass {\n    fn offset(\u0026self, x: f32) {\n        let value = [x, 0.0f32, 0.0, 0.0];\n        if let Some(encoder) = \u0026self.encoder {\n            let pointer = NonNull::new(value.as_ptr() as *mut c_void).unwrap();\n            unsafe { encoder.0.setVertexBytes_length_atIndex(pointer, 16, 0) };\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn point(\u0026self) {\n        if let Some(encoder) = \u0026self.encoder {\n            unsafe { encoder.0.drawPrimitives_vertexStart_vertexCount(MTLPrimitiveType::Point, 0, 1) };\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nhaxe/Main.hx:\n\n```haxe\nimport haxe.io.Bytes;\n\nclass Main {\n\tstatic var sink = 0;\n\n\t/** Median nanoseconds per operation of `run`, which performs `count` operations. **/\n\tstatic function measure(count:Int, run:Void-\u003eVoid):Float {\n\t\tvar samples = [];\n\t\trun(); // warm up: JIT compilation and caches\n\t\tfor (_ in 0...7) {\n\t\t\tvar start = haxe.Timer.stamp();\n\t\t\trun();\n\t\t\tsamples.push((haxe.Timer.stamp() - start) * 1e9 / count);\n\t\t}\n\t\tsamples.sort(Reflect.compare);\n\t\treturn samples[3];\n\t}\n\n\tstatic function report(label:String, ns:Float) {\n\t\tSys.println(StringTools.rpad(label, \" \", 44) + StringTools.lpad(Std.string(Math.round(ns * 10) / 10), \" \", 9) + \" ns\");\n\t}\n\n\t@:noCompletion static function haxeCall(value:Int):Int {\n\t\tsink += value;\n\t\treturn sink;\n\t}\n\n\tstatic function main() {\n\t\tvar count = 1000000;\n\t\tvar probe = new Probe();\n\t\tvar bytes = Bytes.alloc(16);\n\t\treport(\"Haxe static function (no crossing)\", measure(count, () -\u003e for (i in 0...count) haxeCall(i)));\n\t\treport(\"crossing: static, no arguments\", measure(count, () -\u003e for (_ in 0...count) Probe.nothing()));\n\t\treport(\"crossing: method on a handle\", measure(count, () -\u003e for (_ in 0...count) probe.touch()));\n\t\treport(\"crossing: int in and out, exclusive borrow\", measure(count, () -\u003e for (i in 0...count) probe.add(i)));\n\t\treport(\"crossing: 16 bytes in\", measure(count, () -\u003e for (_ in 0...count) probe.bytes(bytes)));\n\n\t\tvar pass = new Pass();\n\t\tvar draws = 10000;\n\t\tvar stream = Bytes.alloc(draws * 4);\n\t\tfunction sample(encode:Void-\u003eVoid):Float {\n\t\t\tvar samples = [];\n\t\t\tfor (round in 0...8) {\n\t\t\t\tpass.begin();\n\t\t\t\tvar start = haxe.Timer.stamp();\n\t\t\t\tencode();\n\t\t\t\tvar ns = (haxe.Timer.stamp() - start) * 1e9 / draws;\n\t\t\t\tpass.finish();\n\t\t\t\tif (round \u003e 0)\n\t\t\t\t\tsamples.push(ns);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tsamples.sort(Reflect.compare);\n\t\t\treturn samples[3];\n\t\t}\n\t\treport(\"Metal draw: two calls (offset, draw)\", sample(() -\u003e for (i in 0...draws) {\n\t\t\tpass.setOffset((i % 64) / 64);\n\t\t\tpass.draw();\n\t\t}));\n\t\treport(\"Metal draw: one call (offset and draw)\", sample(() -\u003e for (i in 0...draws) pass.setAndDraw((i % 64) / 64)));\n\t\treport(\"Metal draw: Haxe stream, one replay call\", sample(() -\u003e {\n\t\t\tfor (i in 0...draws)\n\t\t\t\tstream.setFloat(i * 4, (i % 64) / 64);\n\t\t\tpass.replay(stream);\n\t\t}));\n\t\treport(\"Metal draw: encoded in Rust alone\", sample(() -\u003e pass.drawsInRust(draws)));\n\t\tpass.close();\n\t\tprobe.close();\n\t}\n}\n```","files":null}]}